{{also|Lint}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|linet}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|linette||grain of flax}}, diminutive of {{m|fro|lin||flax}}; or, from {{etyl|Medieval Latin|en}} {{m|la|linteum}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|līnum||flax}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/lɪnt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪnt|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# a [[fine]] [[material]] made by [[scraping]] [[cotton]] or [[linen]] [[cloth]]; used for [[dressing]] [[wound]]s
# [[clinging]] [[fuzzy]] [[fluff]] that clings to fabric or [[accumulate]]s in one's [[pocket]]s or [[navel]] etc.
# the [[fibrous]] [[coat]] of thick [[hair]]s covering the [[seed]]s of the [[cotton]] [[plant]]

